Package: STPGA
Type: Package
Title: Selection of Training Populations by Genetic Algorithm
Version: 7.0.0
Date: 2025-07-27
Author: Deniz Akdemir
Maintainer: Deniz Akdemir <deniz.akdemir.work@gmail.com>
Description: Modern genetic algorithms for optimal subset selection in high-dimensional prediction problems. 
    Provides efficient single and multi-objective optimization for training population selection with 
    comprehensive criteria including A-, D-, E-optimality, prediction error variance (PEV), Cook's distance (CD), 
    and distance-based measures. Features adaptive mutation, tournament selection, diversity preservation, 
    and numerically stable matrix operations. Includes both modern clean interfaces and legacy compatibility functions.
License: GPL-3
Depends: R (>= 3.5.0), AlgDesign, scales, scatterplot3d, emoa, grDevices, parallel
Suggests: R.rsp, EMMREML, quadprog, UsingR, glmnet, leaps, Matrix, testthat (>= 3.0.0), 
    knitr, rmarkdown
VignetteBuilder: knitr
NeedsCompilation: no
Encoding: UTF-8
RoxygenNote: 7.3.1
